Web design pricing in Cardiff is all over the place. You can find someone willing to build a website for £300, and a large agency quoting £10,000 for the same brief. Understanding what drives that variation — and knowing what's actually worth paying for — is how you avoid getting stung.

Here's a straightforward breakdown of web design costs in Cardiff and what you should realistically expect at each level.

## What affects the cost of a Cardiff website?

Before looking at price ranges, it helps to understand what you're actually paying for. The main factors that affect web design cost are:

**Complexity and number of pages** — A five-page brochure site costs less than a twenty-page service site with a booking system, gallery, and blog. The more content and functionality, the higher the cost.

**Custom design vs templates** — A designer who builds your site from scratch will charge more than one who adapts an off-the-shelf theme. But the result is a site that's unique to your business, not one that looks like a hundred others.

**SEO foundations** — Some designers include on-page SEO as standard. Others don't touch it, leaving you with a website that looks great but can't be found. Always ask what's included.

**Who's doing the work** — A large Cardiff agency with account managers, project managers, and multiple departments has higher overheads than an independent studio. You pay for that structure whether it adds value to your project or not.

**Ongoing costs** — Hosting, maintenance, and support aren't always included in the upfront price. Make sure you understand the full cost of ownership, not just the day one cost.

## Cardiff web design price ranges

**From £199 — One-page WordPress starter site**

This is where NC Digital's entry-level builds sit. A focused one-page WordPress website gives your business a professional online presence without the cost of a larger multi-page build. The dedicated [affordable website design Cardiff](/web-design-cardiff/) page explains what's included for local businesses that need a clear starting point.

It's a genuinely professional result at a lower price point — not a throwaway template, but a purposefully built site using the right tools. Well-suited to small businesses that need a solid, fast, SEO-ready starting point.

**£800–£2,500 — Independent designer / small studio**

This is where you'll find independent Cardiff web designers and small studios like NC Digital. You get a properly custom-designed website, on-page SEO foundations, and someone who actually knows your business before they start building. Most small business websites in Cardiff sit in this range.

**£2,500–£6,000 — Complex projects**

Larger sites with [ecommerce functionality](/services/ecommerce-development/), custom integrations, booking systems, or multiple service areas fall into this bracket. The complexity justifies the cost — but make sure the additional features are things you actually need.

**£6,000+ — Large agency territory**

At this level you're paying for agency overheads as much as the work itself. For most Cardiff small businesses, this budget can be better spent on a well-built site plus ongoing SEO investment.

